# Lantern Ward (district_helios_lantern_ward)

Authored plan only. Read-only; no runtime registration, task claim, or gameplay acceptance.

Sector: sector_helios_prime
Existing zones: zone_helios_core, zone_helios_memorial, zone_helios_freight

## Premise
A working harbor neighborhood tends the lamps of a convoy that never came home; its residents also need breakfast, coolant and a way through the afternoon traffic.

## Arrival
A lamp-lighter pulls alongside a dark berth while a passenger shuttle yields to a slow memorial tow. A repair arm works on a damaged shutter. The player sees who is waiting for whom before any job is offered.

## Geometry
A crescent of inhabited hulls around the existing Memorial Array, one public promenade route, an outside freight bypass and a narrow service cut. Keep the training claim and its departure corridor clear. The empty cradle is readable from all three routes.

## Landmark: The Empty Plinth
Existing reference: poi_memorial
Retain the canonical memorial; build an inhabited crescent and a tow cradle around it. The missing lamp belongs to a living family, not a new unexploded-bomb story. The serviced family lamp and cradle are an adjoining new object; the Candle Fleet's canonical dark twenty-fifth memorial plinth remains dark and keeps its identity.

## Population proposal
Normal live demand: 12; alert: 18; finite reserve: 4; shared hard cap: 40. These are plan budgets, not measured performance or guaranteed slot grants.
Planning envelopes, not raised runtime defaults. The current default shared budget is 24; any denser admission must coordinate existing owners and demonstrate cost. Reserve is finite logical inventory, not additional simultaneous bodies.

## Resources
- res_helios_lamp_charge: Finite lamp service cells supplied by an ordinary freight delivery; no cosmetic source creates stock. [economy: src/systems/economy.js]
- res_helios_work_parts: Physical repair parts reserved once for an attended repair. [cargo: src/systems/cargo.js]
- res_helios_berth_service: Durable service state of the affected lamp/berth, not a second commodity. [worldRecords: src/world/worldRecords.js]

## Visible routines

### routine_helios_lamplighter: Lamplighter tender
Owner: npcJobsRuntime (src/systems/npcJobsRuntime.js)
Setup dependencies: none
Inputs: res_helios_lamp_charge
Outputs: res_helios_berth_service
1. Collect one cell at the freight platform.
2. Travel the public service loop with visible cargo.
3. Clamp at the adjoining family lamp, never the canonical dark twenty-fifth plinth; articulated service and a visible crew worker follow the actual native work phase.
4. Consume the cell only on confirmed service, light that lamp, return.
Interruption: Threat pauses service and causes retreat with the same cell. A destroyed lamp cannot be lit by a timer.
Recovery: Recover the same cell or obtain a new paid delivery; damaged mount needs repair.

### routine_helios_shuttle: Shift shuttle
Owner: npcJobsRuntime (src/systems/npcJobsRuntime.js)
Setup dependencies: none
Inputs: none
Outputs: none
1. Open the passenger gate at its actual berth.
2. Wait while the slow tow crosses.
3. Depart along the promenade to the other dock.
4. Return on the next calendar shift, with stop lights and dwell.
Interruption: An obstructed lane yields or takes the signed bypass; passengers never unload into empty space.
Recovery: Physical obstruction removal reopens the normal route.

### routine_helios_repair: Yard repair crew
Owner: npcJobsRuntime (src/systems/npcJobsRuntime.js)
Setup dependencies: none
Inputs: res_helios_work_parts
Outputs: res_helios_berth_service
1. Fetch a part.
2. Brace beside the real damaged shutter.
3. Work while attached; show arm contact and sparks only during service.
4. Leave a visibly restored shutter and a service receipt.
Interruption: Unlatching interrupts progress. Damage creates salvage once; no repair-from-distance.
Recovery: Retain damage and consumed-stock history across departure and Continue.

## Opportunities

### lw_helios_empty_plinth: The Empty Plinth
- Escort the family tow to the empty cradle during ordinary traffic.
- Borrow the tow cradle and move the disabled lamp yourself.
- Clear the service cut so the crew can finish without you.
Committed outcome: The exact lamp is secured at the matching cradle with its native service state restored; one local remembrance unlocks.
Failure: A broken lamp becomes a repair/recovery task. Missing the procession does not erase the family or restart time.
Return visit: The light is on, the family tow has a new berth and a shuttle now uses the reopened route.

### lw_helios_shift_change: Five Minutes Late
- Move the fallen traffic mast.
- Escort the shuttle through the freight bypass.
- Leave it alone and watch the tug resolve the obstruction later.
Committed outcome: Actual shuttle arrival releases its existing schedule; no money for merely entering the area.
Failure: Causing a collision earns a witnessed liability and visible repair demand.
Return visit: Shuttle driver recognizes help or nuisance; the mast remains damaged until repaired.

### lw_helios_borrowed_cradle: Borrowed, According to You
- Ask the yard keeper for the portable tow cradle after helping.
- Take the unclamped cradle during shift change and accept local theft consequences.
- Buy the released surplus cradle when its work is complete.
Committed outcome: Ownership/custody changes through the native object and crime owners; no cloned inventory reward.
Failure: A failed theft becomes retrieval or restitution rather than a reload.
Return visit: Your stored cradle remains the same object; its original berth is empty or supplied with a visibly delivered replacement.

